<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65716" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μειλίσσω</span></b> , fut. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξω</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			A.R.
			4.416
		</span></i>: 
			Ep.
		
		aor.
		
			Med.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μειλίξατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.650
				</span></i>
			: —<i>make mild, soothe, treat kindly</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				16.28
			</span></i>; esp. <i>appease, propitiate</i>: rarely c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρὸς μειλισσέμεν</span> (like <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρὸς χαρίζεσθαι</span>) <i>to appease</i>
			[the dead] <i>by</i> fire, i.e. funeral rites, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				7.410
			</span></i>; of rivers, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιπαροῖς χεύμασι γαίας
				. . μειλίσσοντες οὖδας</span>
			<i>gladdening</i> the soil with rich streams, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				1029
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργὰς μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1339
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τινὰ λοιβαῖς,
			χύτλοις</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				542
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.708
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>implore</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγὼ κεῖνόν γε τεὰς ἐς
				χεῖρας ἱκέσθαι μειλίξω</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				416
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μειλίσσομαι</span>”
				<i>to be soothed, grow calm, h. Cer.</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					290
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be subdued</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρὸς μειλίσσετ᾽ ἀϋτμή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.531
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>use soothing words</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδέ
				τί μ᾽ αἰδόμενος μειλίσσεο μηδ᾽ ἐλεαίρων</span>
			<i>extenuate</i> not aught from respect or pity, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.96
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>propitiate</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύπριν ἀοιδῇσιν θυέεσσί τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.860
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συκοφάντας ἀπομαγδαλιᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					7.23
				</span></i>
			; <i>soften, subdue</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθνη . . καθάπερ ζῷα τιθασεύων καὶ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.330b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>implore</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.985
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.1012
			</span></i>.</div>
